<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Elbow</h1>
<p>Weapon skill
Class: Assassin (guild level 8), Barbarian (guild level 8, up to 60%), Fighter (guild level 8, up to 60%), Thief (guild level 8, up to 90%)
Practising it needs dexterity 40.
Also taught by: Jojun the weapon master, in the west hall of the Huashan Temple near Xiyang City (members of the Fighters', Thieves' and Assassins' guilds only, from level 8)
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre> elbow &lt;character&gt;
 elbow              (whoever you are fighting)
</pre>
<p>This command will allow you to elbow your opponent. It is more powerful when your
hands are free: a shield, a held item or a wielded weapon each make it weaker,
and a two-handed weapon most of all.
</p><p>Elbow is a weapon skill; you must have practised it to elbow. Each elbow costs
2 endurance, and it lands best on someone who isn't fighting yet. It hurts
lightly armoured foes most and does little against plate. You can elbow another
player only when both of you have signed the book of blood.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
